  (jolt-invoke4 (var-deref "clojure.core" "attach-core-doc-meta!") "clojure.core" "cond->>" "Takes an expression and a set of test/form pairs. Threads expr (via ->>)\n  through each form for which the corresponding test expression\n  is true.  Note that, unlike cond branching, cond->> threading does not short circuit\n  after the first true test expression." (jolt-list (jolt-vector (jolt-symbol #f "expr") (jolt-symbol #f "&") (jolt-symbol #f "clauses")))))
(guard (e (#t #f))
  (jolt-invoke4 (var-deref "clojure.core" "attach-core-doc-meta!") "clojure.core" "condp" "Takes a binary predicate, an expression, and a set of clauses.\n  Each clause can take the form of either:\n\n  test-expr result-expr\n\n  test-expr :>> result-fn\n\n  Note :>> is an ordinary keyword.\n\n  For each clause, (pred test-expr expr) is evaluated. If it returns\n  logical true, the clause is a match. If a binary clause matches, the\n  result-expr is returned, if a ternary clause matches, its result-fn,\n  which must be a unary function, is called with the result of the\n  predicate as its argument, the result of that call being the return\n  value of condp. A single default expression can follow the clauses,\n  and its value will be returned if no clause matches. If no default\n  expression is provided and no clause matches, an\n  IllegalArgumentException is thrown." (jolt-list (jolt-vector (jolt-symbol #f "pred") (jolt-symbol #f "expr") (jolt-symbol #f "&") (jolt-symbol #f "clauses")))))
(guard (e (#t #f))
  (jolt-invoke4 (var-deref "clojure.core" "attach-core-doc-meta!") "clojure.core" "conj" "conj[oin]. Returns a new collection with the xs\n    'added'. (conj nil item) returns (item).\n    (conj coll) returns coll. (conj) returns [].\n    The 'addition' may happen at different 'places' depending\n    on the concrete type." (jolt-list (jolt-vector ) (jolt-vector (jolt-symbol #f "coll")) (jolt-vector (jolt-symbol #f "coll") (jolt-symbol #f "x")) (jolt-vector (jolt-symbol #f "coll") (jolt-symbol #f "x") (jolt-symbol #f "&") (jolt-symbol #f "xs")))))
